# .npmignore
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE IS CURRENTLY INERT. It is a safety net, not an active filter.
#
# package.json declares an allow-list:
#
#     "files": ["dist", "docs", "examples", "README.md", "CHANGELOG.md",
#               "CONTRIBUTING.md", "SECURITY.md", "LICENSE", "llms.txt", "llms-full.txt"]
#
# When `files` is present, npm packs only what that list allows and does not
# consult `.npmignore` at all — not for root paths, and not for paths *inside* a
# listed directory either. Verified against this package: an explicit
# `docs/API.md` entry here changes nothing, because `files` already includes `docs`.
#
# So the rules below currently exclude nothing. They exist for the case where the
# allow-list is weakened or removed — a mis-edit that drops `dist` or `docs`, or a
# future maintainer who simplifies `files` away. If that happens this file starts
# working and keeps sources, tooling, local scratch and test output out.
#
# To make it active, delete the `files` field from package.json. Do not do that
# casually: `files` is what keeps the published surface small and explicit, and
# `scripts/copy-extra-files.mjs` verifies the entries it lists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — these are published on purpose. Excluding any of them
# either breaks the consumer (LICENSE) or fails the build outright, because
# copy-extra-files.mjs verifies each one exists and is non-empty:
#
#     LICENSE          the MIT terms a consumer redistributes
#     CHANGELOG.md     what changed, and when
#     README.md        the entry point npm renders on the package page
#     SECURITY.md      the vulnerability disclosure route
#     CONTRIBUTING.md  the changeset and gate requirements
#     docs/            the API, architecture and configuration references
#     examples/        the tiered per-framework guides
#     llms.txt, llms-full.txt
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- repository metadata and tooling -----------------------------------------
.git
.github
.changeset
.kilo
.vscode
.idea
# Instructions for agents working in this repository. Not a consumer document, so it has no
# place in `node_modules`; the consumer-facing conventions are README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md.
AGENTS.md

# --- sources, tests and build scripts (the build output is dist/) ------------
src
test
tests
e2e
scripts
coverage

# TypeScript configuration at the repository root only. The leading `/` is load-bearing: a bare
# `*.ts` matches `dist/index.d.ts` too, so an unanchored rule removes every declaration from the
# tarball and leaves a package that answers every import with `Cannot find module '…' or its
# corresponding type declarations`. `dist/` is published whole and is never filtered here.
/*.ts
/*.tsx
/*.mts
/*.cts
tsconfig.json
tsup.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
vitest.setup.ts
playwright.config.ts
biome.json
commitlint.config.js

# --- package manager artifacts and caches ------------------------------------
node_modules
.npm-cache
.pnpm-store
.pnpm-cache
.size-tmp
.knip-cache
.vitest
.yarn
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
npm-shrinkwrap.json
pnpm-workspace.yaml

# --- test and coverage output ------------------------------------------------
.nyc_output
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
size-limit-report.json

# --- documentation media -----------------------------------------------------
# README.md references the GIF over a raw.githubusercontent.com URL, so it must stay
# in the repository. It is multi-megabyte and nothing imports it, so it has no place
# in the tarball. The frames and pipeline scripts that produced it are local-only.
assets
assets/gif-src
dist/assets

# --- images and stylesheets --------------------------------------------------
# No runtime asset is imported by the package; `files` ships only dist/ plus docs.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.svg
/*.webp
/*.gif
styles

# --- local-only scratch ------------------------------------------------------
# A developer's own copy of the README, worktrees, tarballs, backups and temp dirs.
README copy.md
*.tgz
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.pylibs

# --- environment and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
